    { "dot": "cyan", "title": "Semantic Authority", "items": [
      "Semantic Kernel (K1/K2/K3) is frozen and demonstrated across M0-M10",
      "Canonical Semantic Profile is architecturally required but not yet specified — a disclosed residual, not a built layer",
      "Pure Core evaluates under the Kernel; it never redefines what a Module's ruleset means"
    ] },
    { "dot": "emerald", "title": "Meaning vs. Execution", "items": [
      "Upper layers may express protocol meaning. They may not redefine protocol meaning.",
      "Runtime commits and dispatches; it never re-derives authority once fixed",
      "Providers translate an authorized Outcome into mechanism-specific execution against chains, bank rails, and counterparties, and report back — a report is an Assertion, never world truth"
    ] },
    { "dot": "rose", "title": "SDK Adapter Boundary", "items": [
